(in-package "ACL2") ; added by Matt K. to make this a certifiable book

; E3-a: stock ACL2 hangs (infinite loop in raw Lisp) on the first world-extending
; event after the compiled-lambda cache ring fills up.  No trust tag, no
; skip-proofs, no cl-cache-init: the ring keeps its shipped default size of 1000.
; Needs no books at all (apply$ on a primitive-only lambda is built in).
; EXPECT-AFTER-FIX: reaches "MARK after-table-NO-HANG" and terminates.
; On stock ACL2 it never reaches "MARK after-table-NO-HANG" and spins at 100% CPU.
; (set-inhibit-output-lst '(proof-tree prove event summary)) ; commented out by Matt K.: not an event
; NO cl-cache-init: the cache keeps its shipped default size of 1000.
; (cw "MARK start~%") ; commented out by Matt K.: not an event
